are mentally ill by some definition.

00:08:09.390 --> 00:08:10.390
I don't know.

00:08:10.390 --> 00:08:15.130
I don't know what the standard should be,
the tough one, but I'm willing to hear from

00:08:15.130 --> 00:08:16.830
people in the audience.

00:08:16.830 --> 00:08:20.930
Aaron wrote in and writes in about CNN's right
turn.

00:08:20.930 --> 00:08:25.180
Aaron says, Hi, David, I'm a progressive,
possibly a little to your left on some issues.

00:08:25.180 --> 00:08:30.900
But I have to say that I'm not scandalized
by CNN's decision to drop the Big Lie moniker,

00:08:30.900 --> 00:08:33.529
even though it's very clearly a big lie.

00:08:33.529 --> 00:08:37.649
Don't you agree that the term sounds quite
editorialist thick for a news segment?

00:08:37.649 --> 00:08:43.300
I'm not convinced that a commitment to more
neutral language is, in fact, a turn to the

00:08:43.300 --> 00:08:44.300
right.

00:08:44.300 --> 00:08:45.300
No, listen.

00:08:45.300 --> 00:08:48.600
On the CNN right turn, it's no one thing.

00:08:48.600 --> 00:08:51.819
It's not over dropping the big lie alone.

00:08:51.819 --> 00:08:56.769
It's a combination of things, including statements
made by the new CEO or president, whatever

00:08:56.769 --> 00:08:59.290
he calls himself.

00:08:59.290 --> 00:09:02.819
The big lie thing is one element changes the
staffing.

00:09:02.819 --> 00:09:04.720
It's a lot of different things.

00:09:04.720 --> 00:09:05.920
Recent comments from anchors.

00:09:05.920 --> 00:09:11.610
I would never make the case that just based
on not using the term big lie anymore.

00:09:11.610 --> 00:09:12.829
CNN is now FOX News.

00:09:12.829 --> 00:09:15.660
That wouldn't be accurate.

00:09:15.660 --> 00:09:17.220
It's not what I believe.

00:09:17.220 --> 00:09:22.300
But go back to the segment I did on it, and
it's a much bigger picture issue than that.

00:09:22.300 --> 00:09:25.360
Rodney wrote in about abortion and said Hello.

00:09:25.360 --> 00:09:30.990
Should a registered or voting Republican be
allowed to get an abortion in the United States?

00:09:30.990 --> 00:09:37.410
I get the point of this question if you vote
against abortion being legal.

00:09:37.410 --> 00:09:43.029
By voting for elected officials who will try
to make it illegal should you be allowed to

00:09:43.029 --> 00:09:44.629
get an abortion.

00:09:44.629 --> 00:09:51.619
It is so outside of any legal framework to
deny abortions based on how people vote.

00:09:51.619 --> 00:09:53.110
That my opinion is.

00:09:53.110 --> 00:09:54.589
Here's here's my thought, Rodney.

00:09:54.589 --> 00:09:55.589
Okay.

00:09:55.589 --> 00:09:57.680
And I really appreciate the message.

00:09:57.680 --> 00:10:00.700
